title: WordlistLoader ClearFake ClickFix Delivery Chain
id: b5dc9e46-57b0-422e-9961-e91fc4707053
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the ClearFake ClickFix delivery chain documented by
    researchers (August 2026): a compromised website displays a fake
    CAPTCHA overlay; when the victim pastes the copied command into
    the Windows Run dialog, conhost.exe spawns a hidden cmd.exe that
    launches rundll32.exe to load a DLL from a WebDAV share. The DLL
    is WordlistLoader, an intermediate payload that hides shellcode
    inside English word lists before delivering Amatera Stealer.
references:
    - https://www.gbhackers.com/wordlistloader-amatera-stealer/
    - https://www.gbhackers.com/clearfake-fake-captcha-wordlistloader/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/20
tags:
    - attack.t1189
    - attack.t1684
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1055
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_conhost_cmd:
        ParentImage|endswith: '\conhost.exe'
        Image|endswith: '\cmd.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'rundll32'
    selection_rundll32_webdav:
        Image|endswith: '\rundll32.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '\\'
            - 'webdav'
            - '@SSL'
            - 'dav'
        CommandLine|contains: 'rundll32'
    condition: 1 of selection_*
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate WebDAV-mapped drives loaded via rundll32 in enterprise environments
    - IT automation scripts that use conhost for hidden command execution
level: high
